    "answer": {
      "short": "$c=\\pm4,\\ \\pm\\sqrt5$. Divisors: $x-4$, $x+4$, $x-\\sqrt5$, $x+\\sqrt5$. Solve $(c^2-16)(c^2-5)=0$.",
      "worked": "By the remainder theorem, $P(c)=-10$.\n$$\\begin{align*}c^4-21c^2+70&=-10\\\\c^4-21c^2+80&=0\\\\(c^2-16)(c^2-5)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $c^2=16$ or $c^2=5$, giving $c=4,-4,\\sqrt5,-\\sqrt5$.\nThe corresponding divisors are $x-4$, $x+4$, $x-\\sqrt5$ and $x+\\sqrt5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
